                <pb facs="0256" n="168" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg168"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Conger to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1904-06-08"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">June 8,
                    1904</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Conger reports the killing of Lewis L. Etzel in junk at sea by Chinese
                    soldiers; body is now at Niuchwang. Further information is expected from
                    Miller.)</p>
            </div>
